<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-6256] Fix resource leaks in SparkInterpreterLauncher.detectSparkScalaVersion</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-6256</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Description&lt;br/&gt;
The `detectSparkScalaVersion` method in `SparkInterpreterLauncher.java` contains resource leaks that can lead to file descriptor exhaustion and temporary file accumulation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Bug Details&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Current Implementation Issues:&lt;br/&gt;
1. Unclosed FileInputStream: Line 277 creates a FileInputStream that is never closed&lt;br/&gt;
2. Undeleted Temporary File: Line 273 creates a temporary file that is never deleted&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160; Impact&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Resource Exhaustion: Repeated interpreter restarts can exhaust file descriptors&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Disk Space: Temporary files accumulate in the system temp directory&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;System Stability: Can destabilize Zeppelin if interpreters are frequently restarted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&#160; Root Cause&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The method uses IOUtils.toString(InputStream, Charset) which does not close the provided stream, and there&apos;s no cleanup logic for the temporary file.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
